              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "A cosine splits into equal half-coefficients at $+\\omega$ and $-\\omega$. Here $A=7$, $\\omega=2$, and $\\phi=-\\pi/5$, so the phase enters the coefficients as $e^{-j\\pi/5}$ on the $+2$ term and $e^{j\\pi/5}$ on the $-2$ term.",
